CORE
main.c
--unwind 3 --rounds 2 --por --allow-pointer-unsoundness --mutex-shadow --datarace --no-assertions
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
With --mutex-shadow the state of a mutex is kept in arrays of its own,
indexed by the mutex address; locking must behave as with the state laid
over the program's mutex.
